			"seed": 1339873715,
			"version": 217,
			"versionNonce": 505306355,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1780976979354,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     MONITORING LOOP (every 60 mins)              │\n│  Streamlit app polls Snowflake for:                             │\n│  • Failed jobs (status != SUCCESS)                              │\n│  • Long-running queries (start_time set, no end_time, > 60 min) │\n│  • DMF / data quality failures                                  │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │ Issue detected\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n        │  STEP 1: POST ALERT TO TEAMS                                    │\n│  • 🔴 Job Failure alert  OR                                     │\n│  • 🟡 Long-Running Query alert  OR                              │\n│  • 🔵 Expensive Query identified                                │\n│  Include: job name, query ID, error/duration/cost, dashboard URL│\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 2: COST ANALYSIS (for long-running / expensive queries)   │\n│  • Run cost SQL (§5) to quantify credits used                   │\n│  • Classify as CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW                   │\n│  • Include cost estimate in Teams alert                         │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 3: DIAGNOSE & DRAFT IMPROVEMENT PLAN (per issue)          │\n│  • Separate plan for each failure / long-runner / costly query  │\n│  • Use §6.1 checklist + §6.2 template                          │\n│  • State assumptions, changes, risks, success criteria          │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 4: POST PLAN TO TEAMS FOR REVIEW                          │\n│  • 🟢 Plan posted with Approve / Request Changes buttons        │\n│  • Answer questions / clear confusion in thread                 │\n│  • If changes requested → revise plan → re-post as [FINAL]      │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │ Developer clicks APPROVE\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 5: POST FINAL PLAN & CONFIRM APPROVAL                     │\n│  • Post [FINAL] plan to Teams channel                           │\n│  • Record approver name + timestamp                             │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 6: CREATE FEATURE BRANCH                                  │\n│  git checkout -b perf/<job-name>-<YYYYMMDD>                     │\n│  (fix/ for failures, perf/ for long-running, cost/ for cost)    │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 7: DEBUG & FIX CODE (§8.2 loop)                          │\n│  • Reproduce → apply fix → verify query profile                 │\n│  • Surgical changes only (§9.3)                                 │\n│  • Run DMF / Streamlit assertions                               │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 8: RAISE PR                                               │\n│  • PR description includes before/after metrics                 │\n│  • Links to Teams approval thread                               │\n│  • Post PR link back to Teams channel                           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘",
			"fontSize": 27.85399999999999,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     MONITORING LOOP (every 60 mins)              │\n│  Streamlit app polls Snowflake for:                             │\n│  • Failed jobs (status != SUCCESS)                              │\n│  • Long-running queries (start_time set, no end_time, > 60 min) │\n│  • DMF / data quality failures                                  │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │ Issue detected\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n        │  STEP 1: POST ALERT TO TEAMS                                    │\n│  • 🔴 Job Failure alert  OR                                     │\n│  • 🟡 Long-Running Query alert  OR                              │\n│  • 🔵 Expensive Query identified                                │\n│  Include: job name, query ID, error/duration/cost, dashboard URL│\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 2: COST ANALYSIS (for long-running / expensive queries)   │\n│  • Run cost SQL (§5) to quantify credits used                   │\n│  • Classify as CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW                   │\n│  • Include cost estimate in Teams alert                         │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 3: DIAGNOSE & DRAFT IMPROVEMENT PLAN (per issue)          │\n│  • Separate plan for each failure / long-runner / costly query  │\n│  • Use §6.1 checklist + §6.2 template                          │\n│  • State assumptions, changes, risks, success criteria          │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 4: POST PLAN TO TEAMS FOR REVIEW                          │\n│  • 🟢 Plan posted with Approve / Request Changes buttons        │\n│  • Answer questions / clear confusion in thread                 │\n│  • If changes requested → revise plan → re-post as [FINAL]      │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │ Developer clicks APPROVE\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 5: POST FINAL PLAN & CONFIRM APPROVAL                     │\n│  • Post [FINAL] plan to Teams channel                           │\n│  • Record approver name + timestamp                             │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 6: CREATE FEATURE BRANCH                                  │\n│  git checkout -b perf/<job-name>-<YYYYMMDD>                     │\n│  (fix/ for failures, perf/ for long-running, cost/ for cost)    │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 7: DEBUG & FIX CODE (§8.2 loop)                          │\n│  • Reproduce → apply fix → verify query profile                 │\n│  • Surgical changes only (§9.3)                                 │\n│  • Run DMF / Streamlit assertions                               │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  STEP 8: RAISE PR                                               │\n│  • PR description includes before/after metrics                 │\n│  • Links to Teams approval thread                               │\n│  • Post PR link back to Teams channel                           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
